cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  sc: a pure-Rust reimplementation of the q2-sample-classifier RandomForest
  workflows
abstract: >-
  sc reimplements the RandomForest classification and regression workflows of
  q2-sample-classifier (Bokulich et al. 2018) in pure Rust, usable as a Rust
  library, a WebAssembly module, or through a reentrant Apache-Arrow-based
  C-API. It is statistically equivalent to q2-sample-classifier — validated
  against oracle fixtures generated from a pinned QIIME 2 / scikit-learn
  environment — and bit-reproducible for a fixed (data, seed) on every
  platform, including wasm32.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-07-09'
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: 'https://github.com/the-miint/sc'
authors:
  - family-names: McDonald
    given-names: Daniel
    email: d3mcdonald@health.ucsd.edu
    affiliation: University of California San Diego
keywords:
  - random forest
  - machine learning
  - microbiome
  - qiime2
  - rust
  - webassembly
  - reproducibility
message: >-
  sc is a reimplementation, not an original method. If you use sc in published
  work, please cite the q2-sample-classifier paper (Bokulich et al. 2018,
  doi:10.21105/joss.00934) — the first reference below — which describes the
  workflows sc reproduces, along with scikit-learn (Pedregosa et al. 2011),
  whose RandomForest semantics both implementations follow. Cite this software
  entry in addition if the specific implementation matters to your work (e.g.
  for reproducibility or provenance).
references:
